{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 269,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We all know that light bends when it travels\nthrough glass, water, or other transparent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4100,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "material - that's how a microscope, lighthouse\nand spectacles work!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7350,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you might even know that light bends because\nit travels slower through glass or water than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11370,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through air - but why does light slow down?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13760,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how does it speed up again when it comes\nout on the other side?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16370,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's nothing there to give it a push!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if you think light is a wave, it's easy\nto explain - electromagnetic waves simply"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22360,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travel slower through glass than through air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24390,
    "dDurationMs": 3649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the wave crests are closer to each other,\nbut the light still oscillates the same number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28039,
    "dDurationMs": 2441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of times per second - it stays the same color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30480,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the wave hits the air again, its color\nstays the same, while its crests spread out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34810,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it returns to light speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36370,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The simplified explanation is that the energy\nof a wave is determined by its frequency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39850,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or color, which doesn't change!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41630,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it doesn't need a boost to speed up at\nthe other side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44510,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait, you say!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45510,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought light traveled at the same speed\nin every reference frame - you still haven't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48370,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explained how it can slow down!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49750,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, now let's think about light as a particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52570,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When light goes through glass, it gets knocked\naround and bumps into all sorts of molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56320,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and electrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57320,
    "dDurationMs": 3759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So whenever it's traveling, it's traveling\nat the speed of light - but it's busy interacting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61079,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with and scattering off lots of stuff along\nthe way, and it doesn't necessarily take the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64619,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shortest path through the glass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66759,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like the President of the United States\ntrying to cross a room – if the room is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70639,
    "dDurationMs": 2131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "empty, he can walk across directly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72770,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the room is full of people all of whom\nwant to shake the President's hand, even though"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76209,
    "dDurationMs": 4711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he walks from person to person at full \"Presidential-speed\",\nhe'll get slowed down along the way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80920,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As soon as he reaches the far side of the\nroom, though, he's free to resume his pace."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85049,
    "dDurationMs": 8420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Full speed ahead, Mr. President!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
